  "description": "The canonical READCARD baseline: the whole card master, read and printed in a single pass, and the case the other nineteen in this folder are measured against. app/jcl/READCARD.jcl:22 is a bare //STEP05 EXEC PGM=CBACT02C - grep -c PARM over that job is 0 - so no job parameter is declared, and its single //CARDFILE DD at :25-26 is the only dataset seeded. The dataset is addressed by the CARDFILE binding key that application.yml resolves at record-length 150, never by a dataset name, so no DSNAME literal appears in this file (gate G46). WHAT THIS CASE PINS ABOVE ALL ELSE: the unit under test is account.AccountBalanceReaderJob - an Account-named class in the account package - yet CBACT02C reads the CARD file and never touches the account file. app/cbl/CBACT02C.cbl:29-33 is SELECT CARDFILE-FILE ASSIGN TO CARDFILE, ORGANIZATION INDEXED, ACCESS MODE SEQUENTIAL, RECORD KEY FD-CARD-NUM, over an FD of FD-CARD-NUM X(16) plus FD-CARD-DATA X(134) = 150, and :45 is COPY CVACT02Y. AAP rule R1 governs - the name comes from the prompt, the behaviour comes from the source - and the divergence is catalogued in the register at AAP 0.8.4. A reviewer who trusts the class name will author the wrong twenty cases. THE RUN is :70-87 exactly once. :71 displays the start banner. :72 performs 0000-CARDFILE-OPEN, whose OPEN INPUT at :120 reports '00', so :121 takes its first arm and :126-127 CONTINUE. :74-81 then performs UNTIL END-OF-FILE = 'Y': each iteration READs at :93, lands on the CARDFILE-STATUS = '00' arm at :94, and :78 displays CARD-RECORD - the 01 group item, so the whole 150-byte area including FILLER. :96 is a COMMENT and adds no second line per record, and no 1100-DISPLAY paragraph exists, so one record yields exactly one line. The 51st READ reports '10', :99 moves 16 into APPL-RESULT, :107 finds the 88-level APPL-EOF true and :108 moves 'Y' into END-OF-FILE, so the loop ends without a 51st display. 9000-CARDFILE-CLOSE reports '00' at :139, :140 SUBTRACT APPL-RESULT FROM APPL-RESULT leaves zero, the end banner follows at :85, and GOBACK at :87 leaves RETURN-CODE 0. In repository terms: startBrowse '00', then readNext '00' fifty times followed by '10', then endBrowse '00' (gate G47). The job is driven at tasklet/step level, with no JobLauncher and no HTTP in the path (gate G51). MESSAGE ARITHMETIC: 1 start banner + 50 record images + 1 end banner = 52 ordered DISPLAY_LINE entries. The banners are 38 and 36 characters; every image between them is exactly 150. RECORD GEOMETRY, taken mechanically from app/cpy/CVACT02Y.cpy (RECLN 150), one-based and cumulative, so a reviewer can check this file against the copybook without running anything: CARD-NUM X(16) at 1-16 and also the RECORD KEY, CARD-ACCT-ID 9(11) at 17-27, CARD-CVV-CD 9(03) at 28-30, CARD-EMBOSSED-NAME X(50) at 31-80, CARD-EXPIRAION-DATE X(10) at 81-90 - carrying the copybook's own misspelling, never corrected - CARD-ACTIVE-STATUS X(01) at 91, and FILLER X(59) at 92-150. 16+11+3+50+10+1+59 = 150, so every image ends in 59 spaces; those spaces are significant and must not be trimmed (gates G19 and G21). The copybook declares no COMP-3, no PACKED-DECIMAL and no S9, so every numeric span is unsigned zoned DISPLAY and there is no sign overpunch to model. ENCODING is US-ASCII, named explicitly rather than left to a platform default. NOTHING IS WRITTEN: expectedWrites and expectedFinalState are empty because :120 opens INPUT and the program contains no WRITE, REWRITE or DELETE - SYSOUT at READCARD.jcl:27 is its only output - and no normalisation is declared, because carddata.txt rows are already the full 150 bytes CVACT02Y declares. PROVENANCE: every expected value here is STATICALLY DERIVED by structured reading of app/cbl/CBACT02C.cbl, cross-checked against app/cpy/CVACT02Y.cpy for each offset and width, app/jcl/READCARD.jcl for the step and DD contract, and the real app/data/ASCII/carddata.txt for the fifty seeded rows. It was NEVER captured from a live COBOL execution: AAP 0.7.6 proves that impossible in this environment with eight independently verified blockers - no z/OS runtime, the available compiler's indexed file handler disabled, subprogram linkage that cannot be made executable, a copybook that will not parse, no Language Environment CEE services, no CICS emulator plus three absent IBM copybooks, EBCDIC fixtures needing binary handling, and no alternative compiler installable - and the substitution is recorded as risk R-A. Fifty records in, fifty-two lines out, RETURN-CODE 0.",
